attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 2, `yfeC` to `nupC`, are carried by 91 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 1% of calls {S1}. The model names 76 to 99% of them, fewest at column 2, `nupC`, 76% {S1}.

@variable **A fork at column 3, `hypothetical protein`, is carried by 49%** {S2.c3}. Then columns 4 to 12, `mntH` to `ptsP`, are [[fructose transport]] {S3, Q}. A second branch of 5 families runs through columns 31 to 35, share 17 to 28%, all shell {S8.b31}. The `yfc` genes, columns 41 to 47, are [[fimbrial proteins]] {S8.c41-47, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 78%, and hesitates less there, 0.32 against 0.83 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 35, `yfdF`, a fork column, 2.10 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in variable columns.** Columns 68 to 74, `ubiX` to `rpnB`, are carried by 42 to 59% {S8.c68-74}. The last column is `yfcD`, in 16% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 84% of genes**, 0.65 bits on average, perplexity 2.1 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.79 against 0.25 bits, and names fewer genes, 54% against 95% {C}.

